  "verdict": "NO WIRES \u2014 free ballistic flight at lunar gravity",
  "headline": "Both jumps fit constant-acceleration free fall at g = 1.68 and 1.67 \u00b1 0.11 m/s\u00b2 (lunar g = 1.62) with ~2 mm residuals; no rigid-body tension event, against a changepoint test that would catch a 11 cm/s velocity impulse 95 % of the time (what little residual structure exists moves helmet and backpack oppositely \u2014 limb motion, not a cable), rise/fall symmetric to a few %, and no line above the helmet down to a ~0.8 mm dull-wire visibility bound.",
  "impressive": "The fit residuals exposed the video's own history: a 5-frame periodic timing pattern, identical in both jumps to ~1 ms, showing the clip passed through a 24 fps film-transfer stage with 2:3 pulldown \u2014 recovered blind from the jump dynamics. Correcting it collapses the residuals four-fold to ~2 mm, and what remains is incoherent between helmet and backpack (limb articulation, not any force on the body)."
